[104.26664, "o", "    ✗ bash — exit 1\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 5 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/; echo ---; python3 -m ensurepip -v 2>&1 | tail -20; echo ---; python3 -m pip --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/; echo ---; python3 -m ensu…\r\n    ✗ bash — exit 1\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 6 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip -v -U --default-pip 2>&1 | tail -25; echo ---; python3 -m pip --version 2>&1; echo ---; pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m ensurepip -v -U --default-pip 2>&1 | tail -25; echo ---; py…\r\n    ✗ bash — exit 1\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 7 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip --uninstall 2>&1; echo ---; ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/; echo ---; python3 -m ensurepip --default-pip 2>&1 | tail -10; echo ---; ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ | head; echo ---; python3 -m pip --version 2>&1; pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python"]
[104.266749, "o", "3 -m ensurepip --uninstall 2>&1; echo ---; ls /usr/local/lib/pyt…\r\n    ✗ bash — exit 1\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 8 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info; python3 -m ensurepip --default-pip 2>&1 | tail -8; echo ---; ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ | head; echo ---; python3 -m pip --version 2>&1; pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info; p…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --quiet six 2>&1 | tail -3; python3 -c \"import six; print('six', six.__version__, 'importable')\"; pip3 uninstall -y six 2>&1 | tail -2 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --quiet six 2>&1 | tail -3; python3 -c \"import six; print…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-27b — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\nFixed. Here's what was wrong and what I did:\r\n\r\n**Diagnosis:** Your Python 3.13 install at `/usr/local` had a *corrupt pip record*."]
[104.266769, "o", " The `site-packages` directory contained only `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` (the metadata) — the actual `pip/` package files were missing. So:\r\n- `pip` / `pip3` → `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'`\r\n- `python3 -m pip` → same\r\n- Worse, `python3 -m ensurepip` (the usual repair) kept saying \"Requirement already satisfied\" and did nothing, because it trusted the leftover dist-info.\r\n\r\n**Fix:**\r\n1. Removed the stale record: `rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info`\r\n2. Reinstalled pip from the bundled wheel: `python3 -m ensurepip --default-pip` → \"Successfully installed pip-24.3.1\"\r\n\r\n**Verification:**\r\n- `pip3 --version` and `python3 -m pip --version` both report `pip 24.3.1`\r\n- Round-trip test: `pip3 install six` → `import six` works → `pip3 uninstall six` → clean\r\n\r\nOne optional follow-up: pip itself suggests upgrading to 26.3 (`pip install --upgrade pip`) — not required, but available.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.8-27b tools=10 surface=1ff9b2b7005d\r\n"]
